is the 'Match Engine,' another rectangular box responsible for matching buy=
 and sell orders.  Between the Order Manager and the Match Engine are two v=
ertically stacked rectangular boxes labeled 'Inbound Sequencer' (top) and '=
Outbound Sequencer' (bottom), depicted as arrays of vertical lines suggesti=
ng a queue-like structure.  Arrows indicate the flow of information: the Or=
der Manager sends data to both Sequencers; the Inbound Sequencer forwards d=
ata to the Match Engine, and the Match Engine sends data back to the Order =
Manager via the Outbound Sequencer.  This suggests that the Sequencers mana=
ge the order of processing and communication between the Order Manager and =
the Match Engine, likely handling sequencing and potentially buffering data=
 to ensure efficient and ordered processing." loading=3D"lazy" width=3D"500=
" height=3D"157" decoding=3D"async" data-nimg=3D"1" src=3D"https://bytebyte=
