eys and associated `PriceLevel` objects as values. Each `PriceLevel` appear=
s to be a doubly linked list of orders (`DoubleLinkedList&lt;Order&gt; orde=
rs`), represented visually by boxes containing `Order` objects with `before=
` and `after` pointers indicating their position in the list.  Orders are c=
haracterized by their `quantity`.  A new buy order (e.g., `price =3D 100.07=
, quantity =3D 200`, labeled 1) is added to the appropriate `PriceLevel`'s =
linked list.  A matched buy order (e.g., `price =3D 100.08, quantity =3D 50=
0`, labeled 2) is removed from its `PriceLevel`'s list.  Order cancellation=
 (e.g., `price =3D 100.06, quantity =3D 400`, labeled 3) involves first fin=
ding the order in a separate `HashMap&lt;OrderID, Order&gt; orderMap` and t=
