ent receiving 'orders' as input. These orders are then 'dispatch'ed to an '=
Application Loop Thread,' depicted as a stack of horizontal rectangles repr=
esenting multiple tasks.  This thread processes the orders and sends 'updat=
e' information to an 'Order State' component, which presumably stores the c=
urrent state of all orders.  Crucially, the Application Loop Thread is 'pin=
 to CPU 1,' indicating it's assigned to a specific CPU core, possibly for p=
erformance optimization.  A small matrix to the right of the CPU assignment=
 shows a possible representation of CPU core assignments, with '1' highligh=
ted, confirming the thread's pinning.  After processing, the 'Application L=
oop Thread' 'dispatch'es the results to an 'Output Thread/Netloop,' which t=
hen sends out the processed 'orders.' The entire process is enclosed within=
