<p>Let=E2=80=99s briefly examine the leader election process. The leader se=
nds heartbeat messages (AppendEnties with no content as shown in Figure 21)=
 to its followers. If a follower has not received heartbeat messages for a =
period of time, it triggers an election timeout that initiates a new electi=
on. The first follower that reaches election timeout becomes a candidate, a=
nd it asks the rest of the followers to vote (RequestVote). If the first fo=
llower receives a majority of votes, it becomes the new leader. If the firs=
t follower has a lower term value than the new node, it cannot be the leade=
r. If multiple followers become candidates at the same time, it is called a=
 =E2=80=9Csplit vote=E2=80=9D. In this case, the election times out, and a =
new election is initiated. See Figure 22 for the explanation of =E2=80=9Cte=
rm.=E2=80=9D Time is divided into arbitrary intervals in Raft to represent =
normal operation and election.</p>
